      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 19th century, wealthy New Yorkers built sprawling country estates along Long Island’s Gold Coast, including the area now known as Roslyn Estates.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roslyn_Harbor%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Roslyn Harbor’s name blends a Scottish‑inspired “Roslyn” with “Harbor” to honor its closeness to Hempstead Harbor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roslyn_Harbor%2C_New_York",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Cedarmere, once William Cullen Bryant’s estate, has been transformed into a public park and nature preserve in Roslyn Estates.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
